          "marking": { "correct": 4, "incorrect": -1 },
          "question": "A particle moves in a straight line with constant acceleration $a = 2\\text{ m/s}^2$. If its initial velocity is $u = 3\\text{ m/s}$, find the displacement $s$ after $t = 4\\text{ s}$.",
          "options": ["$20\\text{ m}$", "$28\\text{ m}$", "$16\\text{ m}$", "$32\\text{ m}$"],
          "correctOption": 1,
          "solution": "Using $s = ut + \\frac{1}{2}at^2 = (3)(4) + \\frac{1}{2}(2)(4)^2 = 12 + 16 = 28\\text{ m}$."
        },
        {
